# <%= current_page.data.title %>

The Container Platform is a shared Kubernetes platform for deploying and
running containerised applications. Clusters are organised by business unit and
separated into production and non-production workloads.

The platform uses a GitOps deployment workflow. You declare your application,
environment, and access requirements in Git, then open a pull request. When it
is merged, ArgoCD deploys the workload to the target cluster and keeps the
cluster aligned with the configuration in Git.

